      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-esc">Escalation path (55%):</strong> Houthi naval blockade enforcement (F3, 80%) and 13+ nights of US airstrikes without ceasefire (F1, 10% YES — 90% not halted) drive the active escalation trajectory; a confirmed Aramco facility strike or major Hormuz mining event would breach the $110 Brent threshold (F4, 42%).</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-prot">Protracted path (30%):</strong> Both sides are calibrating within a KIA-ceiling — IRGC struck Al Udeid with injuries not fatalities; the IAEA invitation (F5, 35%) and the Oct 1 ceasefire track (F6, 35%) maintain structural prerequisites for settlement without forcing a decisive outcome.</p>
      <p class="scenario-line"><strong class="label-desc">De-escalation path (15%):</strong> Formal ceasefire by Oct 1 (F6, 35%) or IAEA physical access by Sept 15 (F5, 35%) are the two structured exits from active warfare; the June 17 MOU cycle — from comparable impasse to signed deal in 16 days — holds as the precedent for rapid turnaround.</p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ========== 5. INSIDE IRAN (descriptive, ~200 words) ========== -->
  <div class="section" id="inside-iran">
    <h2 class="section-title">
      Inside Iran
      <span class="meta">State-media decode · ~200 words · verb-ban + forecast-cite rule applies</span>
    </h2>
    <div class="inside-iran">
      <div class="iran-media-badges">
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRNA</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">IRIB</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Press TV</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Fars</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Tasnim</span>
        <span class="iran-media-badge">Kayhan</span>
      </div>
      <p>Iranian state media IRNA and Tasnim framed the ongoing US air campaign this week as "an act of war by an occupying power against a sovereign nation's infrastructure." Coverage of the July 17 IRGC strike on Al Udeid Air Base in Qatar — injuring four US personnel — received front-page treatment in Kayhan. Grossi's July 25 IAEA invitation statement received a short factual item on IRNA's international page, without reference to Iran's prior withdrawal of inspector access or the conditions attached to the current invitation. → supports <span class="cite">F5</span></p>

      <p>Mojtaba Khamenei has made no verified public appearance in 139 days since his assumption of the Supreme Leader role on March 8, 2026. Iranian state media published three written statements attributed to him this week, each prefaced with the title "Ayatollah" — a title he did not hold at appointment and which requires formal clerical conferral. Press TV and IRIB read these statements on air without accompanying video or photograph of him in either broadcast. → moved <span class="cite">F2</span></p>

      <p>Khuzestan province experienced a 36-hour power outage July 20–21, confirmed by Fars News Agency. State media attributed the disruption to US strike damage to the Ahvaz power substation. Iran's Atomic Energy Organization (AEOI) released a statement July 24 asserting that all enrichment facilities are "fully intact and operational" — a rebuttal to US claims that nuclear infrastructure was damaged in the July 9–13 strike cycle. → <span class="context-only">context only</span></p>
    </div>
  </div>

